{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall take for Me a contribution.</b> One may say that this pericope was spoken during the forty days mentioned above, shortly after Moses went up the mountain to receive the tablets and the rest of the Torah, and the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded him to make a Tabernacle, and within it an ark, and inside the ark he would place the tablets." "<b>You shall take My contribution.</b> Rashi's comment: they donated thirteen things mentioned in the passage, and these are: gold, silver, copper, blue, purple, scarlet, linen, goats, rams, tahash skins, acacia wood, oil, spices. And the fragrant spices are included in the oil, since they are not visible, and the princes brought the stones." "<b>[And they shall take for Me</b> — for My name, so that it be for My name]."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:17.672490443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}